7.1.1 Are membership profiles complete (summing to 1)?
For each source unit, interpreter, and round, assigned fuzzy memberships across candidate EFGs should sum to 1.0 (IUCN 2025). The code below sums memb within each (VEGCODE, expert, round) group and filters for totals below 0.999 (allowing minor floating-point tolerance):

TASVEG_clean |&gt;
    group_by(VEGCODE, expert, round) |&gt;
    summarise(total = sum(memb), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
    filter(total &lt; 0.999) |&gt;
    arrange(total) |&gt;
    print.data.frame(digits = 3)

[1] VEGCODE expert  round   total  
&lt;0 rows&gt; (or 0-length row.names)


Only a single assessment falls below 1.0—inspecting Jayne_Balmer’s records for HSE (Eastern alpine sedgeland) shows a Round 2 total of 0.90 across three candidate EFGs:

TASVEG_clean |&gt;
    filter(expert == "Jayne_Balmer", VEGCODE == "HSE")

&lt;membership_tbl&gt;
source_id column: VEGCODE
target_id column: EFG
membership column: memb
interpreter column: expert

# A tibble: 3 × 5
  VEGCODE EFG    memb expert       round
  &lt;chr&gt;   &lt;chr&gt; &lt;dbl&gt; &lt;chr&gt;        &lt;dbl&gt;
1 HSE     T6.4   1    Jayne_Balmer     1
2 HSE     T6.4   0.95 Jayne_Balmer     2
3 HSE     TF1.7  0.05 Jayne_Balmer     2


We retain this record transparently rather than editing the original elicitation input; downstream functions handle it explicitly (for example, summarise_membership() normalises by total membership weight, and calc_shannons_entropy() emits a warning and internally re-normalises vectors whose sum is below 1).


7.1.2 Do any membership profiles exceed 1?
Next, we verify whether any (VEGCODE, expert, round) total exceeds 1.001, which could indicate duplicate entries or arithmetic errors during data entry:

TASVEG_clean |&gt;
    group_by(VEGCODE, expert, round) |&gt;
    summarise(total = sum(memb), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
    filter(total &gt; 1.001) |&gt;
    arrange(total) |&gt;
    print.data.frame(digits = 3)

[1] VEGCODE expert  round   total  
&lt;0 rows&gt; (or 0-length row.names)


No totals exceed 1.001.


7.1.3 Are there duplicated (VEGCODE, EFG, expert, round) rows?
Even when a profile sums to 1.0, an interpreter might inadvertently enter the same target EFG twice in separate paired columns. The code below counts rows per (VEGCODE, EFG, expert, round) combination and flags any count greater than 1:

TASVEG_clean |&gt;
    group_by(VEGCODE, EFG, expert, round) |&gt;
    summarise(n = n(), .groups = "drop") |&gt;
    filter(n &gt; 1) |&gt;
    arrange(n) |&gt;
    print.data.frame(digits = 3)

[1] VEGCODE EFG     expert  round   n      
&lt;0 rows&gt; (or 0-length row.names)


